# An allow-list: the image build (Dockerfile at this root) sees only what
# `cargo build --locked -p swirldb-server` needs, which is the workspace
# manifest and lockfile and every member's manifest and sources.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!native/swirldb-core
!native/swirldb-client
!native/swirldb-server
!tests/Cargo.toml
!tests/integration
# The browser module, for a consumer that builds it from this directory as a
# named context: Swirl Lighting Studio's interface image does
# (`--build-context swirldb=...`), and a named context is filtered by this
# file too, so without these lines the crate is invisible there. The crate
# is outside the workspace and carries its own lockfile; nothing else of
# it (pkg/, node_modules/, the wrapper's build) is an input.
!native/swirldb-browser/Cargo.toml
!native/swirldb-browser/Cargo.lock
!native/swirldb-browser/src

# And none of what those directories accumulate.
**/target
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store
native/*/Cargo.lock
!native/swirldb-browser/Cargo.lock
native/swirldb-server/data
**/*.redb
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
